WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:06.306
Dozens of protests erupted

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:08.475
on university campuses and in cities

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:10.377
across China on Saturday.

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:11.511
In an unprecedented

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:12.545
show of defiance

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:13.213
and anger

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:14.014
against the government's

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:16.349
restrictive zero COVID policy,

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:17.384
many shouted for leader

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:19.419
Xi Jinping and the Communist Party

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:21.121
to step down.

00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:22.355
A deadly fire at an apartment

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:23.223
building in the far

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:23.957
western region

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:25.892
of Xinjiang appears to be fueling

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:27.060
the most recent anger

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.094
as video emerged,

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:30.296
which appeared to show lockdown measures

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:31.798
delayed firefighters

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:33.500
from reaching the victims.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:34.801
Now, in an op ed published

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:35.635
Sunday morning,

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:36.169
Chinese state

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:37.737
media calls the current COVID

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:38.772
measures, quote,

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:40.206
scientifically effective.

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:41.107
Saying the public

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:43.143
should have full confidence in them.

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:43.376
All right.

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:44.711
Let's get the latest from CNN's

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:46.846
Beijing bureau chief, Stephen Jiang.

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:47.981
Stephen, we've seen

00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:49.783
isolated protests before,

00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:51.151
but do these seem different

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:53.286
in terms of the size and the scale

00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:56.890
That's why this wave of protests

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:57.690
really triggered

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:58.291
by that

00:00:58.291 --> 00:00:59.526
deadly Xinjiang fire

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:00.126
you just mentioned,

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:02.429
but also how the authorities are handled,

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:03.430
the aftermath,

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:04.164
because on one hand,

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:05.231
they reject the claims

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:06.132
that their

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:06.900
COVID measures

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:07.967
had anything to do

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:09.903
with the firefighters inability

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:11.838
to reach the fire quickly.

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:12.839
But on the other hand,

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:14.874
after insisting for weeks and months

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:16.242
that COVID situation

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:18.244
in Xinjiang was so severe and lockdowns

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:20.313
must be maintained, all of a sudden

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:22.449
they announce this miraculous victory

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:23.583
in their campaign

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:25.385
and also a phased reopening.

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:27.420
So I think all of that really serving

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.321
as the latest

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:29.389
and loudest wake up

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:30.690
call to a lot of people

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:31.191
in terms

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:32.792
of how increasingly

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:34.794
ineffective, unscientific

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:36.763
And not to mention potentially dangerous

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:38.765
this zero COVID that policy has become.

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:40.166
And also, of course,

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:41.401
all the absurdities

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:43.169
surrounding its enforcement.

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:44.370
That's why why

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.205
we have seen people

00:01:45.205 --> 00:01:46.206
across this country

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:47.006
really

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.175
trying to take the matter

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:50.076
into their own hands.

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:51.845
Not only you see people in Xinjiang

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:52.779
taking to the streets,

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:54.314
demanding their freedom,

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:55.982
clashing with security forces,

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:57.350
but also even here in Beijing,

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:57.851
for example,

00:01:57.851 --> 00:01:59.886
residents are seeing tearing down

00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:00.687
metal barriers

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:01.254
or fences,

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:01.588
set up

00:02:01.588 --> 00:02:03.022
a set up by local officials

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:05.458
to seal them off in their residences.

00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:07.560
But all of that really culminating

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.261
Saturday night

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:11.030
into Sunday morning with multiple vigils

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:12.065
and protests

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:13.032
often spearheaded

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:16.102
by young people on university campuses.

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:16.402
You know,

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:18.538
they are seen holding up white paper,

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:19.439
white obviously

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:20.540
being the color of mourning,

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.509
not only for the victims of Xinjiang,

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:23.643
but also trying to,

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:25.645
as they seem to trying to indicate

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:27.580
there was so much anger and frustration

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.582
pent up inside themselves

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:31.050
and that they were not allowed

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:31.818
to express them.

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:32.552
Because, remember,

00:02:32.552 --> 00:02:34.754
for a lot of these university students,

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:37.290
their entire college life has been under

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:39.926
some form of a lockdown can

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:42.061
it's looking at the video.

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:44.030
You see how big the protests are.

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:45.632
You see the police presence there.

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:47.567
You talked about clashes

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:48.401
with authorities.

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:50.103
Is there a chance that the crackdown

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:51.304
on the protests

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:52.572
might turn more violent,

00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:54.240
maybe even deadly

00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:57.544
That is a potential worry

00:02:57.544 --> 00:02:59.479
because when you look at these protests,

00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:01.181
I think they are widespread,

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:01.648
as you mentioned.

00:03:01.648 --> 00:03:03.750
But that one extraordinary protest,

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.318
you place some of the

00:03:05.318 --> 00:03:05.885
the sound

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:07.387
and the introduction was the one

00:03:07.387 --> 00:03:09.422
taking place in downtown Shanghai

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:10.323
on Saturday night

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:11.658
because the protester there

00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:13.426
really chanting slogans directly

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:15.428
targeting the ruling Communist Party

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:17.597
and its strongman leader, Xi Jinping.

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:20.200
That was just such a watershed moment

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.167
in the minds of many people

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:22.235
because so far, even

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:23.836
the opponents of the policy

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:25.371
have been dancing around this

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:26.272
quite a bit in terms

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:26.973
of saying

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:27.874
the policy

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:29.909
may not be all wrong and the leadership

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:30.343
really

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:31.678
their heart was in the right place.

00:03:31.678 --> 00:03:33.446
But blaming local enforcement

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:34.847
and pointing a finger

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:36.015
at as overzealous

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:37.650
or incompetent local officials.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.185
But those protesters in Shanghai

00:03:39.185 --> 00:03:40.353
really directly

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:41.788
challenging the legitimacy

00:03:41.788 --> 00:03:43.690
of the Communist Party and its leader.

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:44.924
That, as you know, is something

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:46.693
simply not tolerated here.

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:47.460
So that's why

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.262
there was a lot of concern, worry

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:50.263
about the protesters.

00:03:50.263 --> 00:03:51.564
Some of them have been taken away

00:03:51.564 --> 00:03:53.533
by by police Windows ten.

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:54.400
That's why

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.970
a crowd has again gathered up in Shanghai

00:03:57.003 --> 00:03:58.104
on the same location

00:03:58.104 --> 00:03:59.205
demanding their release.

00:03:59.205 --> 00:04:00.006
So I think

00:04:00.006 --> 00:04:01.507
there was a lot of concern there,

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:02.642
but not to mention, of course,

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:03.309
from the government's

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:04.978
perspective, there was also a lot of fear

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:07.080
that this kind of chanting and protest

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:09.449
could inspire others across this country.

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:10.650
Yeah, absolutely.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.785
We'll keep an eye on this important story

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:13.653
throughout the morning.

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:14.988
Steven Zhang, thanks so much.

